      "writtenOn": "2024-07-23T08:01:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you please help me understand what would be benefits of this model? It doesn\u0027t look a lot different from current model to me, as long as init_rc and vintf_fragment files are not shared between modules, or may have different characteristics (such as properties or custom genrule) per each file.",
      "parentUuid": "6f061fa9_abbcbaa9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1835,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1840,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "11915238a58cb10c082d3d524f605bc03d12ed6a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49c86481_66bc634c",
        "filename": "android/module.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1840,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T07:18:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We had a discussion about this today. My point was that the way init_rc and vintf_fragments are handled at the moment is very exceptional in Soong, which I think was okay only because \"required\" dependencies were not tracked in Soong then. Since Soong now can correctly track the required dependencies, I think this should be modeled after that. tl;dr; I consider this as a tech debt.\n\nColin, please chime in, as you wrote this. What was your plan on this?",
      "parentUuid": "e35d2993_5e06d0e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1835,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1840,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "11915238a58cb10c082d3d524f605bc03d12ed6a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3a8243f_62000ede",
        "filename": "android/module.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1840,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-24T17:34:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was just maintaining the status quo for how it worked in Make.\n\nSharing a `prebuilt_etc` module seems ideal, but there are 365 mentions of `init_rc:` in Soong.  I don\u0027t think automatically creating a `prebuilt_etc` module helps that much, creating modules is always hard to follow, and you\u0027d still need to do deduping to avoid creating the same `prebuilt_etc` module twice.",
      "parentUuid": "49c86481_66bc634c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1835,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1840,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "11915238a58cb10c082d3d524f605bc03d12ed6a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e390610_e3d36acf",
        "filename": "android/module.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1840,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-31T11:20:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, deduping is required for the auto-generated modules. And, yes they make logs difficult to understand, but I honestly don\u0027t think there actually will be a user error here.\n\nFixing all the 1000+ places (yes, in git_main) at the same time is impossible. So, I suggest we have an allowlist of directories where init_rc and vintf_fragments are allowed, so that new directories are forced to use the prebuilt_etc + required combo.",
      "parentUuid": "f3a8243f_62000ede",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1835,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1840,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "11915238a58cb10c082d3d524f605bc03d12ed6a",
